(5) THE a0-RELEVANCE: r_M = sqrt(G M_b/a0) at group scale

    a0 = 9.3619e-11 m/s^2 (G075 canonical).  M_b = (f_gas,500 + 0.02 stars) M500 from E11 where f_gas measured;
    else f_b = 0.05 assumed.  X-COP cluster comparison: r_M/R500 ~ 0.24-0.31 (G095: R500/r_M ~ 3.2).
    E11 26 groups: r_M(M_b) median 57 kpc, range 20-132 kpc
    r_M(M_b)/R500: median 0.102, range 0.074-0.171   (task's 'large fraction' claim: realized on the M_dyn footing only)
