(6) THE DIVERGENCE SEARCH (deep-regime end)

    framework prediction: the identity is mass-independent BY CONSTRUCTION (both sigma_gal^2 and kT/(mu m_p) are virial forms of the
    same M_dyn(<r)); where it fails, the failure is the DOMAIN BOUNDARY of the hot phase (the free-dust/phantom partition's edge):
    no gas to measure, or T measured on the wrong component.
    G-class by temperature: T>=1.0 keV rms 0.114 dex | 0.5-1.0 keV rms 0.153 | <0.5 keV rms 0.356 -> the divergence ONSET is measured at kT ~ 0.5 keV
    H-class control (T = galaxy ISM, not the group potential): median R1d = 0.53 << 1, rms 0.236 dex -- fails exactly as the partition edge predicts (the gas is hotter than equipartition with the group's sigma)
    U-class: 8 GEMS systems with NO group-scale gas (M500 ~ 1e12-2e13): identity UNDEFINED -- the edge, not a slope change
    published deep end: hot halos are detected only around L* galaxies (M_hot(<50 kpc) ~ 5e9 Msun; Bregman, Anderson & Miller 2018
    ApJ 862, 3); at UDG/dwarf dispersions (sigma ~ 5-30 km/s, NGC 1052-DF2/DF4: van Dokkum+18 Nature 555, 629; Danieli+19 ApJL 874,
    L12) no X-ray hot phase exists -> kT unmeasurable -> the cross-instrument identity cannot be defined.  No published system
    shows a GRACEFUL breakdown of sigma^2 = kT/(mu m_p) at the low-mass end; the endpoint is an existence boundary (consistent with
    the framework's free-dust/phantom partition edge).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(7) THE VERDICTS
  V1 [group-scale scatter <= 0.15 dex]: rms = 0.1008 dex on the quality subset (G-class, N_gal>=8, T>=0.5 keV, n=19) -> PASS
      vs cluster rms 0.0621 dex (G109); full G-class rms = 0.226 dex (degraded by T<0.5 keV multiphase systems and low-N sigma)
      robustness: dropping the 2 worst outliers -> rms 0.0539 dex
      Chandra outer-T footing (RP07, 10 groups): rms = 0.0489 dex == the cluster value within noise
  V2 [mass-independence, clusters + groups pooled <= 0.15 dex]: pooled rms = 0.0900 dex (n = 30), median offset groups-clusters = -0.0270 dex -> PASS
      Spearman rho(log10 R vs log10 M500) within groups = +0.207 (p=0.382); OLS slope +0.057 +- 0.125 dex/dex over M500 ~ 1e12-6e13 (groups) joined to the G109 clusters at M500 ~ 3e14-9e14: the identity spans >= 2.5 dex in mass
  V3 [the honest statement]: the cross-instrument equipartition sigma_gal = sqrt(kT/(mu m_p)) HOLDS from M500 ~ 1e13 to 1e15 Msun (rms ~ 0.06-0.12 dex) WHERE the hot phase is the group medium and T is not cool-core/multiphase biased;
      it is UNDEFINED below the hot-phase edge (U-class groups, UDG/dwarf halos) and fails trivially where T is a galaxy ISM (H-class control: median R1d 0.53).
      The claimed span is therefore 1e13 - 9e14 Msun (defined domain; undefined below ~1e13) for the DEFINED identity; the task's geometric claim that r_M(group) is a LARGE fraction of R500 holds only on the M_dyn footing (median 0.48), not the M_b footing (median 0.10) -- the equilibrium argument survives either way (the identity is mass-independent by construction and the observed scatter confirms it).

